Since April, people have reported bookings landing on the wrong day. The desk merged **412 unique reports** into #4471; the export contained 15 duplicate rows.

The reports describe two separate problems. Both affect tenants whose locale writes the day before the month, but they enter through different date-reading paths.

## Problems

### Shared parser reads day-first dates as month-first — 379 reports

The shared parser reads every date month first. For day-first tenants, an input such as `07/04/2026` is interpreted as July 4 instead of April 7. This is the larger cause group and includes reports from app, email, and form channels.

**GitHub ticket:** [parser: day-first dates are read month-first](https://github.com/beastieskate/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)

### Booking-v3 hint disagrees with the tenant’s date order — 33 reports

The `booking-v3` form displays an `MM/DD/YYYY` hint to tenants whose locale is day-first. People follow the hint, then the form reads the value using the tenant’s day-first convention, so month and day are exchanged.

**GitHub ticket:** [hint: booking-v3 shows the wrong date order](https://github.com/beastieskate/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)

## Counts

| Problem | Reports | Ticket |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Shared parser reads day-first dates as month-first | 379 | #1 |
